window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>One True King Tenebrous Days for Qiledara... The absence of Aaron since he left on his quest troubles his companions. With his whereabouts unknown, the heroes of Qiledara are tested in ways they never could have imagined, and they face an ever-growing threat from beyond the Amber River. Meanwhile, Aaron’s enemies seek to take advantage of his absence for their own gain. Who will remain loyal and steadfast during these dark days, and who will bring the evildoers to justice?</p> <p>Narrated by Garan Patrick, also the voice of King Gautier, Drefon, Brayden, and Governor Gilbert Phillip Nathaniel Freeman as Otheran, Theodamus, Gueric, Lieutenant Griere, the sentinel, all the dragonkin, and other men Zach Brown as Jole, Captain Piers, the pirate captain, old Evrart, a Galdutian prisoner, a stable boy, and the crowd Matthew Biddulph as Aaron the Dragonslayer Robert Cassyleon as Damien Hannah Dere as Elodie, the flower merchants, and other women Louise Porter as Penelope Bobby Gaglini as Timothy the Brave Jody Smith as Odette Cory Barton as Lance Marnie Thomson as Alianora Carolynne Henry as Anna the Diviner and Queen Lysandra James Hernandez as Loman Brad Grochowski as a Bainfaren soldier, Malchom, old Graybeard, General Lorin, a Kereshan independence fighter and the herald Nathan Phoenix as Nathaniel Scott Fins as Makarius, a fisherman, a pirate and other men Jarrett Raymond – a Bainfaren soldier, various soldiers and guards Emily Christine as Queen Meline and Brenda Ged Cartwright as Owen and King Luan Chisomo Burke as Princess Coralie Ellen Cribbs as Cecile, Lady Barbara, Helena, and other women Kevin Casey as Lord Cedric and Lord William Evan Zimmerman as the bard Jenny W. Chan as various children and Rob Sharp as the soldiers from the Hidden Kingdom.</p>"; 
